NAME
    summary - print a free-text state summary of the loaded core

SYNOPSIS
    summary

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the attached core's unstructured free-text state summary from
    the emusen.session service, covering state that does not yet have a
    dedicated inspection command. Prints 'No target attached.' if no game
    is loaded.

    On cores using the stable ABI, the first line identifies the engine,
    system, and current frame number, followed by main-CPU register state
    supplied by the console's system pack (for example, a single-line
    65816 register summary on SNES with active P flags in uppercase).

EXAMPLES
    summary

EXIT STATUS
    0   Summary printed (including when no target is attached).
    1   Session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    regs(1), cpus(1), spaces(1), coretop(1)
